contracts.py, geometry.py and parts of bridge.py are a modified port of files of ASPIRE
(https://github.com/NVlabs/ASPIRE), at commit fa00f0ef2bc1d91d594b9aa502c22133c9f538f7: src/cap_harness/contracts.py,
errors.py, protocols.py, geometry.py, api.py and runtime.py. ASPIRE is under the Apache License 2.0
(https://github.com/NVlabs/ASPIRE/blob/fa00f0ef2bc1d91d594b9aa502c22133c9f538f7/LICENSE).

Positronic changed the port: it takes the joint count of an arm from the rig's state and the embodiment name from a
setting, keeps of the perception types only segmentation and point clouds, keeps of the provider protocols only
text-prompted segmentation, drops the planning types, and lets a camera observation hold RGB without depth,
intrinsics or pose. With no segmentation provider, segment_text raises NotImplementedError, where ASPIRE gives a
result with ok=False. A provider that raises gives a result with ok=False, where ASPIRE lets the exception through.

